────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────                                        
                                                                                                                        
### Bottleneck — Turn 11 (distFromStart 3200–3300 m)                                                                    
                                                                                                                        
Observations:                                                                                                           
                                                                                                                        
- Apex speed: 62.7 km/h at dist 3286 m — the absolute minimum on the entire lap (compared to hairpin apex: 72.8 km/h at 
  dist 2469 m).                                                                                                         
- The car spends 1.84 s in the 35 m band 3265–3300 m at a mean of 67.7 km/h. This is the single most time-expensive     
  section on the track.                                                                                                 
- Peak |trackPos| = 0.813 at dist 3289 m with steer = 1.00 (saturated for 70 consecutive ticks, 3265–3290 m). The apex  
  is against the edge.                                                                                                  
- Braking starts at dist 3140 m with track9 = 126.5 m and car speed 168.9 km/h. Model computes v_target = sqrt((55/3.6)²
  + 2·7.0·126.5)·3.6 = 161.2 km/h → brake = (168.9 − 161.2) / 15 = 0.51.                                                
- Only 4 brake events exceed 0.5 on the whole lap, all in the pre-hairpin zone (2228–2239 m). No heavy braking at T11:  
  the model feathers the brake from 3140 m gradually.                                                                   
- Hairpin (dist 2468 m): apex 72.8 km/h, |trackPos|_max = 0.566, no steer saturation, 0 damage. The hairpin is no longer
  a problem.                                                                                                            
                                                                                                                        
Hypotheses (not confirmed, would require changing BRAKE_DECEL and rerunning):                                           
                                                                                                                        
- BRAKE_DECEL = 7.0 m/s² is conservative: the car successfully decelerates from 168.9 km/h at dist 3140 m to 62.7 km/h  
  by dist 3286 m (a distance of 146 m), which implies an average deceleration of ~9.8 m/s² — substantially higher than  
  the model's assumption of 7.0 m/s². The model is starting braking ~25–40 m earlier than the physics require.          
- If the model trusted a higher deceleration (8.5 m/s²), v_target at d = 126.5 m would be 175.8 km/h > 168.9 km/h →     
  brake = 0, delaying the braking point. The apex speed would be preserved, but the car would carry more speed through  
  3000–3200 m.                                                                                                          
                                                                                                                        
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────                                        
                                                                                                                        
### Proposed change — V3.5                                                                                              
                                                                                                                        
ONE parameter: PARAMS["BRAKE_DECEL"] 7.0 → 8.5 m/s²                                                                     
                                                                                                                        
Mechanism: The braking-distance formula v_target = sqrt(V_CORNER² + 2·BRAKE_DECEL·d) sets the speed ceiling at every    
distance d. A higher BRAKE_DECEL raises v_target at every approach distance, delaying braking points across all corners 
while the apex speed stays fixed (V_CORNER_MIN = 55 km/h). At d = 200 m (sensor cap), target rises 198.3 → 217.0 km/h.  
                                                                                                                        
Expected effect: 0.2–0.5 s saved at T11 alone (braking starts later, entry at ~178 km/h vs 169 km/h); an additional     
0.3–0.6 s across the rest of the lap from higher straight speeds. Apex speeds at hairpin and T11 unchanged.             
                                                                                                                        
Risk: Medium. The hairpin at dist 2468 m (prior crash site) is the most exposed corner: V_CORNER_BONUS ≈ 0 (short ±30°  
rays), so V_CORNER = 55 km/h. With BRAKE_DECEL = 8.5, braking from ~137 km/h to 73 km/h requires ~71 m; current braking 
zone starts at dist 2230 m with 239 m to the apex — adequate margin. The danger is if 8.5 m/s² overstates grip on this  
corner specifically: the result would be a wider apex line, pushing |trackPos| toward 0.7–0.8. |trackPos| > 1.0 means   
crash. Revert to 7.0 if any damage appears or |trackPos| exceeds 0.85 at the hairpin.                                   
                                                                                                                        
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────                                        
                                                                                                                        
